Vendored third-party code
=========================

Component: libmdbx (aka MDBX)
Location: src/vendor/libmdbx
Upstream: https://libmdbx.dqdkfa.ru
Copyright (c) 2015-2026 Leonid Yuriev <leo@yuriev.ru>
License: Apache-2.0

The vendored files are mdbx.c, mdbx.h and mdbx-internals.h -- the three files
that constitute the official libmdbx amalgamation -- together with the upstream
LICENSE, NOTICE and COPYRIGHT, which are retained verbatim in
src/vendor/libmdbx and apply to the files there. libmdbx's command-line tools,
C++ API, test suite and build system are not vendored.

The sources were taken from release tag v0.14.3 (tag object
cf3e13938bf974260872e629713f6ecf30e62030, commit
f7a3a9323cacacfa9dc6137ae7a7252a67744ff0) via upstream's GitHub mirror at
https://github.com/erthink/libmdbx. Per-file SHA-256 digests of the pristine
sources are recorded in .agents/vendoring.md in the package's source
repository.

Local modifications to the vendored sources, which constitute the notice
required by section 4(b) of the Apache License, are confined to
src/vendor/libmdbx/mdbx.c and src/vendor/libmdbx/mdbx-internals.h. They route
libmdbx's panic path through a package-owned guard that marks the owning handle
unusable and raises an R condition instead of calling the platform assert
handler or abort(); send log output through R's console instead of stderr; read
NT_TIB::Self directly rather than through __readgsqword(), which avoids a
false-positive -Warray-bounds from Rtools' MinGW headers; and remove nine
upstream diagnostic-suppression pragmas (#pragma GCC/clang diagnostic
ignored ...), which are unnecessary under R's compilation flags and trip CRAN's
pragma check. Together these ensure no compiled code writes to stderr or
terminates the R process. Each change is also recorded as a patch in
tools/patches/ in the package's source repository. mdbx.h, LICENSE, NOTICE and
COPYRIGHT are unmodified.

